# Tetun orthography for this repo.
#
# `both` is deliberate. client/i18n/locales/tet.ts is genuinely MIXED — it
# carries INL markers (ll, ñ, kept accents) and DIT ones (lh, nh) side by side,
# written over two years by different hands.
#
# `both` is the TOLERANT mode: it reports a divergence from either standard at
# info level and asserts neither. It is also the LOUDEST — on the 2026-08-07
# pass it produced 31 orthography notes (16 ORTH-032 + 15 ORTH-032-INL) where
# `dit` alone produced 16. That is the honest trade: the extra noise is the file
# telling you it has not picked a side, and both directions stay INFO, so real
# ERRORS remain visible. That pass surfaced 14 of them — escaped unicode,
# Portuguese left untranslated, and a `maié`/`maibé` typo.
#
# Pinning INL or DIT would turn several hundred existing, correct strings into
# findings overnight. Choosing for real is a product decision needing a native
# reviewer and a one-off sweep of the whole file, not a lint setting. Until
# then this file exists so nobody has to remember the flag.
ortho: both
